.TH QWFILE 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwfile \- smart file, remote URL, and hierarchical codebase analyzer using local Qwen3-4B
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwfile
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIpdf\fR|\fItxt\fR|\fIcode\fR]
[\fB\-\-web\fR]
[\fB\-\-keep\fR]
[\fB\-\-export\fR \fIpath\fR]
\fItarget\fR
[\fIprompt\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwfile
is an intelligent terminal inspection and analysis tool powered by a locally hosted, uncensored Qwen3-4B model.
It accepts local files, remote HTTP/HTTPS URLs, GitHub repositories, fuzzy project aliases, or entire source directory trees.
.PP
Depending on whether
.I target
is a single file, a remote resource, or a codebase directory,
.B qwfile
automatically selects the optimal processing strategy:
.TP
.B Single File Analysis
Extracts source code, plain text, or document content (including automated text extraction for PDF files via \fBpypdf\fR, \fBpdfplumber\fR, or \fBpdftotext\fR).
The file content is formatted with syntax fences and passed to the model alongside the user prompt.
.TP
.B Hierarchical Codebase Analyzer
When
.I target
is a directory or a recognized project,
.B qwfile
initiates a structured multi-pass codebase inspection:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
.B Directory Mapping:
Scans the repository structure using recursive directory listing (\fBtree\fR or \fBls\fR) while respecting standard exclusion filters (\fB.git\fR, \fBnode_modules\fR, \fBtarget\fR, \fB__pycache__\fR).
.IP 2. 3
.B Modular Decomposition:
Splits the repository into logical module chunks bounded by context limits (at most 24,000 characters per chunk).
.IP 3. 3
.B Incremental Note Synthesis:
Iteratively inspects each module chunk, extracting architecture patterns, component definitions, and potential vulnerabilities.
Notes are written directly to disk under \fI/tmp/local\-llm/<project>/notes/module_XX.md\fR.
.IP 4. 3
.B Holistic Synthesis:
Aggregates all modular notes into a cohesive final architectural analysis and streams the output directly to the terminal.
Temporary notes are automatically deleted upon completion unless \fB\-\-keep\fR is specified.
.RE
.TP
.B In\-Memory Dependency Symbol Resolver
Prior to analyzing source code files (C/C++ and Python),
.B qwfile
parses top-level \fB#include\fR and \fBimport\fR statements.
Signatures of imported functions, classes, structs, and variables are extracted into a volatile RAM symbol cache (\fBSymbolCache\fR).
Relevance filtering ensures only symbols actually referenced in the target code are injected into the prompt.
The in-memory cache is fully cleared and garbage-collected once inference concludes, preventing memory accumulation.
.TP
.B Smart Target Resolution
If
.I target
does not exist in the current working directory,
.B qwfile
searches active development environments (such as \fI~/Projects\fR, \fI~/Code\fR, or \fI~/src\fR) to resolve fuzzy project names (e.g., \fBmyproject\fR maps to \fB~/Projects/myproject\fR).
Remote Git URLs or shorthand identifiers (e.g., \fBgh:owner/repo\fR) are cloned into temporary storage (with automatic \fBtorsocks\fR routing if Tor is active).
.TP
.B Hybrid Inference Engine
If a local \fBllama\-server\fR is running (default: \fIhttp://127.0.0.1:8080\fR),
.B qwfile
streams tokens via Server\-Sent Events (SSE) through direct HTTP requests.
If the server is offline or busy, it seamlessly falls back to the standalone \fBllama\-cli\fR executable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " tokens"
Set context window size in thousands of tokens.
Accepted values:
.RS
.TP
.B 16
16,384 tokens (~12k words). Fast inference, lowest VRAM footprint.
.TP
.B 32
32,768 tokens (~24k words). Default balanced profile.
.TP
.B 48
49,152 tokens (~36k words). Maximum context for extensive repositories.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-r " level"
Set reasoning effort level (\fI0\fR to \fI4\fR):
.RS
.TP
.B 0
Reasoning off (direct output, fastest response).
.TP
.B 1
Low reasoning (concise thinking phase).
.TP
.B 2
Medium reasoning (default balanced thinking).
.TP
.B 3
High reasoning (thorough step-by-step analytical thinking).
.TP
.B 4
Maximum reasoning (exhaustive chain of thought for deep audits).
.RE
.TP
.BI \-f " format"
Override automatic format detection.
Supported formats: \fBpdf\fR, \fBtxt\fR, \fBcode\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-web\fR, \fB\-\-search
Perform anonymous Tor-isolated web research on detected package dependencies (e.g. from \fIrequirements.txt\fR, \fIpackage.json\fR, \fICargo.toml\fR).
Proprietary project code and local paths are never leaked; only sanitized package names are queried over Tor SOCKS5h.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Preserve intermediate modular notes generated under \fI/tmp/local\-llm/<project>/notes/\fR instead of purging them upon completion.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " path"
Write the final synthesis report to the specified markdown file path in addition to displaying it in the terminal.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command synopsis and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QWEN_DIR
Path to the Local-LLM-Unsensored repository.
Defaults to the location where the suite was installed.
.TP
.B QWEN_PORT
HTTP port for the local \fBllama\-server\fR daemon.
Defaults to \fB8080\fR.
.TP
.B CTX
Manual token context size override passed to backend binaries.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .qwignore
Project-level exclusion file to omit sensitive directories, private files, and proprietary packages from LLM context and Tor research.
.TP
.I ~/.config/qw/ignore
Global user exclusion rules applied across all repositories.
.TP
.I /tmp/local\-llm/<project>/
Temporary workspace directory used by the Hierarchical Codebase Analyzer for chunking and synthesis notes.
.TP
.I prompts/cli_rules.md
System instructions and tool definitions loaded during CLI queries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Analyze a single source file with default parameters:
.RS
.nf
qwfile cll/inference.py "Explain the streaming inference workflow"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Perform a deep architecture audit on a local directory with maximum reasoning:
.RS
.nf
qwfile \-r 4 \-c 48 src/ "Analyze subsystem communication and failure modes"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect a fuzzy-resolved codebase and export findings while keeping intermediate notes:
.RS
.nf
qwfile \-\-keep \-\-export /tmp/audit.md src/ "List all safety failsafes"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze a remote PDF specification without downloading it manually:
.RS
.nf
qwfile \-f pdf https://example.com/datasheet.pdf "Summarize bus interface specs"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect a remote GitHub repository over Tor:
.RS
.nf
qwfile gh:torvalds/subsurface-for-dirk "Explain dive profile calculation"
.fi
.RE
